MID_SE_Esm_Die_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_001: Stupid lid's bent. Maybe if I press here... Nope.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_002: Hey, stop messing with that jar already and hand\nit over. I'd be happy to help.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_003: No one asked you. I'll have this open in a minute\nwithout your help.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_004: Don't be shy! I'll get it for you.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_005: Should only take me a sec. Make with it!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_006: I don't need a stranger's help with a lid that's on\nthe wrong way.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_007: Gods, you're stubborn! I've got this!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_008: Ugh, fine, then. Have at it. Just be careful.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_009: Sure, sure. Alright, just...
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_010: This... This is pretty tight! It's totally stuck.\nOK. Here we go.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_011: Hey, I told you to be careful with that.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_012: Raaah!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_013: Oops. Ehe. Looks like I broke it. Sorry.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_014: Oh, look...ointment. Well, on the bright side, it didn't\nspill everywhere!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_015: Hmph...
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_016: I'm sorry, Diego. Look, I'll pay you back for it.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_017: Don't bother. I can make my own.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_018: The Har Hali have a traditional method of making\nvessels from hollowed-out cadam nuts.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_019: Really? Well, maybe I can help. I'm good with\na knife.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_020: You've helped enough, thanks. No point in making\none just for it to get wrecked again.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_021: So rude! What's his problem, anyway?
MID_SE_Esm_Die_C_022: {SetColor=Gray}Sure, I messed up, but... Maybe I can make it\nup to him.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_001: Oh hey, Diego. There you are. This is for you.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_002: I wanted to replace that jar I broke. Doesn't it\nlook perfect?
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_003: And this one won't warp. Go ahead—it's yours.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_004: It's a nice gesture. But ceramics are brittle.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_005: It could crack in transit, or during a pitched battle.\nSeems like a pretty basic oversight.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_006: Huh?
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_007: It's not completely useless, though. I'll figure\nsomething out.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_008: Is that all you have to say? No "thank you"? 
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_009: What's with the sudden attitude? Did I say\nsomething wrong?
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_010: You have no idea how to talk to people, do you? So\nunfriendly, so superior!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_011: Oh. I see your point. Anyway, I can think of some\nbetter materials than ceramic.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_012: Right back to the jar? I've had enough!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_013: Oops. I kinda threw that. Hard. Too hard!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_014: Not a scratch on it. I might owe ceramic an apology.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_015: Wait, really? Let me see!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_016: Oh good, it's fine! Whew.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_017: {SetColor=Gray}Oh, wow. Now that I get a look at him...he's a cutie!{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_018: Ehehe. Sorry about that. Again. I was trying to\napologize and I almost broke this one too.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_019: Like I said, it was a nice gesture. I'm glad it\ndidn't break.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_020: Hmm? Uh, yeah!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_021: Thanks for thinking of me. I'll put it to good use.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_022: {SetColor=Gray}A thank-you? And he'll find a use for it?{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_023: {SetColor=Gray}Oh, I get it now. He's not a bad guy, he's\njust...awkward.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_024: Maybe I'll wrap it in cord to be on the safe side.\nI'd hate for it to break now.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_025: Oh, I can help with that. I'm good with cord too!\nOn account of growing up in a fishing village.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_026: And I'll do it just like you tell me this time. Promise!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_027: In that case, I wouldn't mind the help.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_028: Alright! It's settled. Let's get to it. I'll go get\nthe cord!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_B_029: She seemed happy. Did I say something...right?
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_001: Oh, Diego! You're hurt! Are you OK?
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_002: Just a minor injury from training. A little ointment\nwill fix it.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_003: Oh, look! That's the jar I gave you. I guess you did\nend up using it!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_004: It's lightweight and easy to carry. And sturdy too,\nafter we reinforced it.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_005: Hehe. That so? I just did what you told me.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_006: {SetColor=Gray}He really is a good guy. He just isn't very sociable.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_007: {SetColor=Gray}And those looks...{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_008: What are you saying?
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_009: Was I talking out loud? Ahaha. I, um... I... Orchel!\nI was just thinking about Orchel!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_010: She's totally beautiful, isn't she? I bet you think so\ntoo, you sly dog!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_011: The thought never crossed my mind. I'm here to\nserve Orchel, not dote on her.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_012: Yes, I'd die for Orchel. But that doesn't mean I'm\ninterested in her like that.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_013: Really? It doesn't? If I were you, I'd tell her\nI love her!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_014: I mean... You're not so bad looking yourself. Right?
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_015: You two would make quite a cute little couple, if I do\nsay so myself!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_016: I've never thought of myself as "cute." That's more\nyour thing.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_017: What? Me? What? What?
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_018: No need to go all flushed. You heard me. I've been\nthinking so since we knelt in those bushes.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_019: Wait, you noticed me when I noticed you? Does that\nmean it's...fate?
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_020: No! Can't be! Fate is for me and my Sweetie!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_021: Oof. What was that for? I was only speaking\nmy mind.
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_022: Well... But... It's your fault! Obviously!
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_023: Are you mad that I told the truth, or are you asking\nme to say it again?
MID_SE_Esm_Die_A_024: Argh! No! Stop talking! And stop looking at me!